Asha closes the door.
Moti immediately becomes restless.
He paces here and there in the flat.
He looks for Asha and whines.
I want to calm him.
I sit down on the rug.
I pat the rug with my hand.
I tell him affectionately, "Moti, come here."
"Come near me and sit here."
He looks at me, but does not come near.
He looks toward the door again.
I take his favourite toy out of Asha's bag.
It is a chew toy.
I show him that toy.
I call him again, "Moti, look at this."
"Take this, this is your toy."
He comes near me slowly.
"Now sit right here."
"Don't worry," I tell him.
He takes the toy and sits near my feet.
He looks a little calmer now.
